I love fixing it.

253
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:04,800
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

254
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:05,960
Whatever this is about, it can wait.

255
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,280
Now, your mother's on her way up the stairs.

256
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:09,440
When she gets here, we all yell, surprise, okay?

257
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:12,920
Jason? Yes, we're up in Ben's room.

258
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:17,020
Not anymore. Surprise!

259
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,120
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

260
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,160
You did all this?

261
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,580
Yeah, well, not just myself.

262
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:25,340
It was everybody.

263
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,340
Everybody except me.

264
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:37,680
Honey? She loves it.

265
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:43,340
I just don't get it.

266
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,400
I thought you'd be so pleased.

267
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,460
We fixed up the nursery.

268
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:47,240
Oh, was it nice gesture, Jason?

269
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,340
Even with the hideous drapes?

270
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:53,920
But what kind of a mother am I going to be if I don't even have time to take part in

271
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:55,080
getting the nursery ready?

272
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:58,180
We have a great one, honey, a sensational one.

273
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,340
Who just doesn't have any taste in drapes.

274
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:04,520
Oh, a great mother would have been able to tell her boss she was pregnant.

275
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:07,140
What? I chickened out.

276
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:09,940
Oh, honey, why are you so afraid to tell him?

277
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:11,060
I am not afraid.

278
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:11,980
I know what it is.

279
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,820
I'm just... scared.

280
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:17,460
Oh. Well, what are you so afraid...

281
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:18,400
so scared of?

282
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:19,960
Well, I don't know.

283
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:23,240
That he'll treat me like I'm pregnant and things are going to change.

284
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,920
Honey, of course things are gonna change.

285
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:26,400
But I don't want them to change.

286
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:28,960
I'm finally fitting in at work, doing a great job.

287
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:31,420
But, sweetheart, we just have to face it.

288
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,360
Now, we're gonna have to make some adjustments.

289
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:39,360
What adjustments? Well, like, uh, like reducing my patient load.

290
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:40,560
Can you do that?

291
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,320
Of course I can.

292
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,400
I just have to start curing those nutso's fast.

293
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,120
What? It's a joke, honey.

294
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:51,140
But we never talked about you scaling down your practice before.

295
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:52,560
Well, I just never thought of it before.

296
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,900
Well, shouldn't you have thought of it before?

297
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:55,580
I guess, I don't know.

298
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:57,380
Oh, great, this kid doesn't have a chance.

299
00:13:57,440 --> 00:14:00,540
She's got a terrible mother and a thoughtless jokester for a father.

300
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:06,400
All right, Benny, I'll admit it.

301
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,980
My plan didn't work out perfectly.

302
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:09,860
Oh, sure it did.

303
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,880
Hey, come on, Benny, I had the best of motives here.

304
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,100
I mean, I wanted Carol to get the short end of the stick.

305
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,980
Ben, you see what happens when you trust Mike?

306
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:21,200
You end up in the guest room.

307
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,740
A guest in your own home.

308
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:28,540
And, boy, might as well just go rent an apartment or something.

309
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:32,440
Hmm. I don't think.

310
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:35,400
I think, Carol, not bad.

311
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:40,420
When Mom and Dad find out about this, and I promise you, they will,

312
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,980
you will be in deep,

313
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:47,600
deep trouble. Look, don't start blaming Ben's housing problems on me.

314
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:49,800
Then whose fault is it?

315
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,820
I think we both know the answer to that one.

316
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:00,940
You're blaming this on an unborn child?

317
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,360
Hey, let's look at the facts here, Carol.

318
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:08,140
I mean, so far this kid who I personally don't even know yet has upset everybody.

319
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:11,560
It is gonna be a girl.

320
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,820
Mike, I'll pray for you.

321
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:20,040
Look, Carol, I mean, nobody bothered to ask me how I felt about having a new kid

322
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:20,760
around this house.

323
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:23,000
Well, so, nobody asked Ben or me, either.

324
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:26,620
Well, all I'm saying is, I mean, if we have family meetings about vacations,

325
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:28,060
shouldn't we have had one about this?

326
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:30,540
You're right. Yeah.

327
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:31,780
You know what I think?

328
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:35,040
I think Mom and Dad are trying to sneak this new kid by us.

329
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:40,100
Now, Mike, we should still have a family meeting.

330
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:42,720
I mean, we obviously have a lot to discuss.

331
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:45,920
I bet Mom and Dad will think it's a great idea, too.

332
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:48,280
They love it when we want to communicate.

333
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:52,320
And I'll be the one who proposed it.

334
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,520
Okay, okay, here's the answer to that problem.

335
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:58,840
When the baby cries at night, I'll be the one who gets it.

336
00:15:58,920 --> 00:15:59,840
No, no, no, no.

337
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,800
You have to look good in front of that news camera.

338
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,120
Without your sleep, you look like death warmed over.

339
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,780
A nice death.

340
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:09,620
But, Jason, Jason, you have to get your sleep, too.

341
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:11,060
You have patients every morning.

342
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:14,700
Oh, sure, but when I look like hell in the morning, my patients feel better about

343
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:17,040
themselves. Isn't that my job?

344
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:19,860
Oh, but what if you resent scaling down your practice?

345
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,140
What if you resent me?

346
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,940
What if you resent the baby?

347
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:27,140
Maggie. Mom, Dad, we need to see her family meeting right now.

348
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,020
I fear for the future of this family.

349
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:31,420
Mike, we're a little busy.

350
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:32,220
Yeah, but Dad, we need to.

351
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:33,300
Come on, Mike.

352
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:36,080
Mom, Dad, we really need to see her family meeting immediately.

353
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:39,120
Trust me. Carol, has your mother just explained to Mike we can't?

354
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,680
Absolutely, Carol. Let's go.

355
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:43,680
What? Dad? What?

356
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:46,340
But you heard your mother.

357
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:51,940
Living room, kitchen, one burr.

358
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:54,800
What the heck's a burr?

359
00:16:57,100 --> 00:17:01,880
Hmm. Swimming pool, TV, refrigerator, no laundry.

360
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:06,640
All right! Ben, what are you doing?

361
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,400
Looking for my own place.

362
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:11,540
What? But sweetheart, why?

363
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:15,100
Well, as long as I've left my room, I might as well get something nice without

364
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,200
flowers on the wall.

365
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,380
Well, how are you gonna pay for this?

366
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:21,920
No problem. See, most of these ads say first months rent free.

367
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:23,420
Well, I'll just move every month.

368
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:27,720
I'd like to call the Siever family meeting to order.

369
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,900
I move that we talk about how Mike conned Ben out of his room.

370
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:32,660
Carol, you have not been recognized.

371
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,560
In fact, I'm not even sure that's you at all.

372
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:37,400
Mike, what did you do to Ben?

373
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:39,680
Dad, I don't believe that's the purpose of this meeting here today.

374
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:42,280
I think what we should be talking about is this baby mess.

375
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:46,140
Baby mess? Mike, this baby is a blessed event.

376
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:48,920
With the sergeant in arms, please escort this lady out.

377
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,840
Mom, Dad, Mike hates the baby.

378
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,780
What? No, no, no, no, no.

379
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:55,040
You have me confused with Ben.

380
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,840
Ben? I just want my room back.

381
00:17:58,340 --> 00:18:00,080
But you volunteered to give it up, didn't you?

382
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:01,960
This meeting is adjourned.

383
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:02,900
Thank you very much for coming.

384
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:03,680
I'm gonna take a leave.

385
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:05,320
It is not.

386
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:06,700
Mike, get back in here.

387
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:10,980
Kids, this new baby is going to change things around here.

388
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:12,520
And some of them are going to be wonderful.

389
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:13,820
Some of them aren't.

390
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:15,920
All you two can think about is yourselves.

391
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:18,880
Personally, I'm going to love everything about this baby.

392
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,580
Even coming home straight after school to help out?

393
00:18:21,780 --> 00:18:25,240
Of course. This wouldn't be every day, would it?

394
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:29,740
No, but Carol, are you ready for things like changing dirty diapers?

395
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:32,280
Oh, I thought Ben would do that.

396
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:36,680
Why me? Because my instinct tells me you'd be good.

397
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,660
I'm not good at it.

398
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,920
Stink is right.

399
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:44,200
Carol, you will be doing your share of changing dirty diapers.

400
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:47,760
Ew! I thought the record show that Ms.

401
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:50,520
Blessed Event here said, quote, ew!

402
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:56,940
All right, now every member of this family is gonna have to make some sacrifices

403
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:58,240
here. Me too?

404
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,100
Yes, you too.

405
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,640
You're gonna have to get used to the new stereo policy.

406
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,020
Okay, okay, all right.

407
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:06,300
My show will be turned off every night by 11 p.m.

408
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:07,520
1 a.m.

409
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:10,300
tops. That's not what we had in mind.

410
00:19:10,740 --> 00:19:11,760
Okay, midnight it is.

411
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:12,840
You can count on me.

412
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:17,400
There will be no music while the baby is asleep day or night.

413
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:18,200
Day or night?

414
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:22,600
What's left? Ben, how do you feel about making sacrifices?

415
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:23,520
It's fine with me.

416
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:25,300
I'm gonna be hanging out in my duplex.

417
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:29,240
I'm still not clear how Ben lost his room.

418
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,080
Mike conned me out of it.

419
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:34,020
Let the record show Mike and I will talk later.

420
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,720
During moonlighting.

421
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:42,580
What I don't get is, why do we have to suffer when you're the one having the baby?

422
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:46,580
Ben, you kids aren't the only ones being asked to sacrifice around here.

423
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:48,400
Your father's gonna rearrange his whole practice.

424
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:51,600
And your mother's gonna take time off from a job she's just getting used to.

425
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:55,940
Well, if this baby's messing everybody up, then why are you having it?

426
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:59,640
Why? Yeah, why?

427
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:04,820
Yeah. Well, I never thought about putting it into words.

428
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,080
That's not easy to do.

429
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:09,100
So you guys don't know either?

430
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,420
Oh, no, no, no.

431
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:12,480
We know. I...

432
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:20,180
Well, I guess because a baby is as close to a miracle as we're ever gonna get.

433
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:25,220
And having each one of you was the most wonderful thing to ever happen to your

434
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:25,940
father and me.

435
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:28,660
Thank you, Mom.

436
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:29,920
That's really beautiful.

437
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:32,720
Especially the way you included Mike.

438
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,760
Carol. Does that answer your question, Ben?

439
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:40,400
No. No. Jason?

440
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:46,720
Yes, well, uh, well, Ben, uh, your mother and I, we believe there's nothing in the

441
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,200
world more important than our family.

442
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,340
We sure do.

443
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:52,140
Not work or losing sleep.

444
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:54,460
Not me reducing my patient load?

445
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:58,700
Nothing. Oh, honey, why didn't we come up with all this upstairs?

446
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,320
I don't know.

447
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:01,900
Oh, Jason, this baby's gonna be great.

448
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,960
That doesn't answer my question either.

449
00:21:07,780 --> 00:21:12,120
I think what Ben's trying to ask here is, what's in this baby deal for us?

450
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:19,780
What's in it for you?

451
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:21,520
It was Ben's question.

452
00:21:23,620 --> 00:21:26,020
Why, everything. The same that's in it for us.

453
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:30,800
Now, you guys insult each other more than anybody I know, but I'd also bet my soul

454
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:33,920
that deep down underneath all of that, each one of you loves each other.

455
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:37,460
Now, Carol, how would you really feel if there were no Mike?

456
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:42,920
Huh? And Ben, how would you really feel if there were no Carol?

457
00:21:44,340 --> 00:21:48,720
Huh? And Mike, what would you really feel if you don't say one word to spoil the

458
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:52,600
sensitive mind? I just think that you're a little bit more sensitive We are all

459
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,920
going to have a new person to love.

460
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:59,880
And once he or she is here, we'll wonder how we ever lived without her...

461
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:04,260
or him. Ben, does that answer your question?

462
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,620
I think so.

463
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:10,620
So you're saying it's not just you and Mom having a baby, we're all pregnant?

464
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:14,440
Well, you couldn't be more right, Ben.

465
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,600
This is so sweet.

466
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:22,680
Oh, Mike, are you crying too?

467
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:25,780
No, it's your feet.

468
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,080
I can't remember when I was more proud of those guys.

469
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:41,820
Oh, yeah, they are finally truly excited about the baby.

470
00:22:42,180 --> 00:22:44,040
And you were wonderful.

471
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:45,340
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

472
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:51,480
Honey, who are you calling at this hour?

473
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:52,300
Oh, my doctor.

474
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:53,340
It's time. What?

475
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:56,980
Just kidding. My boss.

476
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:58,860
Ugh. Why don't you call him tomorrow?

477
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:00,560
No, I don't want to put this off another...

478
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:01,640
Hello? This is Maggie.

479
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,320
I'm calling to tell you I'm pregnant.

480
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:07,520
I'm four months along, but if you still want to put me in a leotard next week, I'm

481
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:11,540
game. This isn't 55512.

482
00:23:40,940 --> 00:23:47,140
I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm gonna be a star I'm

483
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:47,820
gonna be a star
